1
00:00:03,399 --> 00:00:07,560
Fern loved Wilbur more than anything.

2
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:13,959
She loved to stroke him, to feed him, to put him to bed. Every morning, as soon

3
00:00:13,959 --> 00:00:20,918
as she got up, she warmed his milk, tied his bib on, and held the bottle for him.

4
00:00:20,918 --> 00:00:25,158
Every afternoon, when the school bus stopped in front of her house, she

5
00:00:25,158 --> 00:00:30,440
jumped out and ran to the kitchen to fix another bottle for him.

6
00:00:30,440 --> 00:00:36,519
She fed him again at supper time, and again just before going to bed. Mrs.

7
00:00:36,519 --> 00:00:42,679
Arable gave him a feeding around noon time each day when Fern was away in school.

8
00:00:42,679 --> 00:00:48,440
Wilbur loved his milk, and he was never happier than when Fern was warming up a

9
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:55,240
bottle for him. He would stand and gaze up at her with adoring eyes.

10
00:00:55,240 --> 00:01:00,360
For the first few days of his life, Wilbur was allowed to live in a box near

11
00:01:00,360 --> 00:01:05,559
the stove in the kitchen. Then, when Mrs. Arable complained, he was moved to

12
00:01:05,559 --> 00:01:12,440
a bigger box in the woodshed. At two weeks of age, he was moved outdoors. It

13
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:18,039
was apple blossom time, and the days were getting warmer. Mr. Arable fixed a

14
00:01:18,039 --> 00:01:23,240
small yard specially for Wilbur, under an apple tree, and gave him a large

15
00:01:23,240 --> 00:01:26,679
wooden box full of straw with a doorway

16
00:01:26,679 --> 00:01:31,080
